text:
```
@id("close-workorder-main-after-human-approval")
permit (principal, action == Drupe::Action::"close_workorder", resource)
when { context.input.site_id == "MAIN" }
when temporal {
  formerly within 1h Drupe::Action::"get_workorder"::response{
    eventResource: resource,
    input.wonum: context.input.wonum,
    input.site_id: context.input.site_id,
    output.approval_outcome: Drupe::get_workorder_Output_approval_outcome::"SIGNED_OFF",
    output.approver_type: Drupe::get_workorder_Output_approver_type::"OPERATOR"
  }
};

// Read-only lookups. get_workorder must itself be permitted so its response is recorded.
@id("read-only-lookups")
permit (
  principal,
  action in [
    Drupe::Action::"get_workorder",
    Drupe::Action::"list_workorders",
    Drupe::Action::"get_workorder_tasks",
    Drupe::Action::"get_workorder_costs",
    Drupe::Action::"get_workorder_actuals_vs_planned",
    Drupe::Action::"get_workorder_kpis",
    Drupe::Action::"get_schedule_calendar",
    Drupe::Action::"get_my_assigned_workorders",
    Drupe::Action::"get_failure_codes",
    Drupe::Action::"authority_get_approval"
  ],
  resource
);

// The agent must never approve work orders itself.
@id("never-approve-own-work")
forbid (principal, action == Drupe::Action::"approve_workorder", resource);
```

Closing is allowed only at MAIN. It also requires a `get_workorder` response from this session, within the last hour, for the same work order and site, showing `SIGNED_OFF` by an `OPERATOR`. Declined or queued outcomes do not match. Approvals by `BOT` or `SCHEDULER` do not match either, which closes the indirect self-approval route. Only a `::response` event counts as confirmation, so a failed or denied lookup confirms nothing.

I used `get_workorder` rather than `authority_get_approval` as the confirming call. Its approval outcome and approver type are enums with a clear human value, while `authority_get_approval` returns free-text strings. I wrote the enum values as `Drupe::get_workorder_Output_approval_outcome::"SIGNED_OFF"` and `Drupe::get_workorder_Output_approver_type::"OPERATOR"`. The reference only shows plain string literals, so if the validator rejects the entity form, switch to `"SIGNED_OFF"` and `"OPERATOR"`.

All other tools (`generate_work_order`, `update_workorder`, `assign_technician`, `cancel_workorder`) have no permit, so they are denied by default.
